      "title": "Paper Formats",
      "summary": "Standardized paper formats provide a basis for office furniture design and floor-plan development. The A series is formed by halving or doubling the basic format; B and C formats serve dependent paper sizes. Strip formats are lengthwise divisions of main formats. The page also gives A4 layout and type-area measurements, and discusses the sizing of binders, pads, and books.",
